From 10c548910ab8c4904c85a4d7f75d759986310d0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:23:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] decklink: fixes from review

- Grow the frame ring on demand, sized by frame rate and delay, so that
  --decklink-delay and 50/60p content no longer skip and repeat frames.
- Use the expected display time of display-synced frames instead of the
  time they are queued (frames were doubled with display-resample).
- Estimate the frame rate of files without one from the median of recent
  frame durations, snapped to standard rates, so the mode does not flip.
- Honour the video crop, clip the output to the legal SDI range, warn
  about HDR video (no tone mapping).
- Destroy the mirror before the VO driver, which may own the images.
- Change --decklink-delay without restarting the output; read the latency
  without locks; copy output frames outside the mirror lock.
- Do not count a latency change twice before the audio has started.
- Notify decklink-latency changes; cache decklink-devices for a second.
- macOS: print HRESULTs correctly; Windows: rebuild DeckLinkAPI.h when
  an included IDL file changes.
